- 16-key keypad mapped to keyboard (1234/QWER/ASDF/ZXCV), shown in UI
- Demo ROM (byte array) that draws a sprite and reacts to key presses
- File ROM loader
- Run, pause, single step, reset controls
- Adjustable instructions-per-frame speed slider
- Debugger panel showing V0-VF registers, I, PC, stack, decoded current instruction
- All controls functional
- Dark themed, clean UI layout

The demo ROM should be a real assembled CHIP-8 program that:
1. Loads a custom sprite (e.g. a smiley face or simple shape)
2. Draws it at center of screen
3. Allows moving it with WASD or arrow keys (2/4/6/8 on CHIP-8 keypad)
4. Shows key reactivity

The HTML file should have complete inline CSS and JavaScript, no external dependencies.

